; fas9_mtext_width.scr - facit of 9.S (Codex 17): does an MTEXT's width (41, its context's 40) count in $EXTMIN/$EXTMAX, plain and
; annotative at another annotation scale?
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_mtext_width.scr
; starts AutoCAD 2025's core on acad.dwt (a new empty drawing). Plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP (see fas9_example.scr).
;   mtext_width              one MTEXT "A" at 0,0 set in a width of 100 (the text far narrower than its width), REGENALL, ZOOM E
;   mtext_width annotative   the MTEXT erased; an annotative MTEXT "A" at 0,0 in a width of 20 (style HDXF_ANNO, height 3), the scale
;                            HDXF_1_5 added to it, CANNOSCALE HDXF_1_5, REGENALL, ZOOM E (its width there is 100)
_.-MTEXT
0,0
_W
100
A

_.REGENALL
_.ZOOM
_E
;SAVE mtext_width
_.ERASE
_ALL

_.ANNOALLVISIBLE
1
_.ANNOAUTOSCALE
0
_.-SCALELISTEDIT
_Add
HDXF_1_5
1:5
_Exit
_.-STYLE
HDXF_ANNO
txt
_Annotative
_Yes
_No
3
1
0
_No
_No
_No
_.-MTEXT
0,0
_W
20
A

_.-OBJECTSCALE
_ALL

_Add
HDXF_1_5

_.CANNOSCALE
HDXF_1_5
_.REGENALL
_.ZOOM
_E
;SAVE mtext_width annotative
